One file, **four** edits, all in `src/tools/expand/handler.ts` at `dc5a548`.

(1) `Scoped` (`:361-365`), today:
```ts
interface Scoped {
  readonly read_status: ReadStatus;
  readonly coverage: Coverage;
  readonly relation: TotalRelation;
}
```
becomes the same three members plus:
```ts
  /** The graph's own skipped-path count for this generation, from `assemble`: the one number
   * `totals.not_indexed_total` publishes, so no tool derives it from a list it holds. */
  readonly notIndexedTotal: number;
```

(2) `scopeOf` (`:409-423`) returns that field from the `assemble()` result it already has:
```ts
  return {
    read_status: readStatusOf(generation, indexedAt, freshness, now),
    coverage: assembly.coverage,
    relation: assembly.relation,
    notIndexedTotal: assembly.notIndexedTotal,
  };
```
`assemble` (`src/shared/domain/coverage.ts:109-131`) already computes it; this adds no reader call and no SQL.

(3) `coverageSummary` (`:633-642`) stops reading the repo-wide total. New signature and body, keeping the existing wording:
```ts
function coverageSummary(
  payload: CoveragePayload,
  totals: Totals,
  truncated: boolean,
  skipped: number,
): string {
  const shown = payload.files.length;
  const total = totals.files_total ?? shown;
  const head = `coverage for ${payload.prefix}`;
  const body = truncated
    ? `showing ${shown} of ${total} files, ${skipped} not indexed`
    : `${total} files, ${skipped} not indexed`;
  return `${head}: ${body}.`;
}
```
Delete the line `const skipped = totals.not_indexed_total ?? payload.not_indexed.length;`. Add a one-line comment above the function saying why the number is the scope's: the sentence prints beside the list this answer holds, and the graph's total is `totals.not_indexed_total`.

(4) `coverageAnswer` (declared `:1101`, returns at `:1134`): in `totals` replace `not_indexed_total: payload.not_indexed.length,` (at `:1117`) with `not_indexed_total: scope.notIndexedTotal,`; change the two summarize call sites (`:1126` and `:1132`) to `coverageSummary(payload, totals, false, scope.coverage.skipped)` and `(env) => coverageSummary(env.payload, env.totals, env.truncated, env.coverage.skipped)`.

Must not change: `payload.not_indexed` construction, `coverage` (it stays `scope.coverage`, so `coverage.skipped === coverage.not_indexed.length` still holds on an untruncated answer), `files_total`, `total_relation`, `sized`/`emit`, any other `scopeOf` caller (`:732,803,852,906,934,983,1014,1048`), `coverage.tests`, and every other tool. No new payload key, no schema change, no migration, no dependency change.
